{
  "Motif": "ogres",
  "Name": "Ogres",
  "Draw": "Ogres are enormous, thick and slow. A small head sunk into a huge sloped body, a heavy jaw with tusks or broken teeth, tiny deep-set eyes, and a gut. The skin is thick and hide-like, scarred, boil-marked and filthy. They wear whatever is big enough - hides lashed with rope, a barrel or a cauldron worn as armour, iron scraps hammered flat and tied on - and their weapons are found rather than made: a tree, a stone, a wagon axle. Frame them so the body overfills the picture.",
  "ElementDraw": {
    "fire": "Hide blistered and split, soot black up both arms, the end of whatever they are carrying alight. Hot orange light coming up off it.",
    "ice": "Rime over the whole hide, frost in the tusks and the matted hair, breath in enormous plumes. The skin has gone blue-grey.",
    "lightning": "Arcs jump between every iron scrap lashed to the body, the hair stands off the skull, and all the metal is haloed yellow.",
    "earth": "Mud-caked and stone-studded, green rock grown through the hide plates and moss packed into the folds. It reads as half quarry.",
    "arcane": "Violet light comes out of the mouth and the deep-set eyes, the tusks glow from inside, and the silhouette will not hold still."
  },
  "ValidFloors": [
    4,
    8
  ],
